; E1, the pipe. A static archive with a C-callable interface and nothing else.
;
; `foreign_stubs` compiles retrainer_stubs.c INTO the archive, so the C++ side links
; one library rather than a library plus a loose object. The stubs are hand-written
; CAMLprim, not ctypes: every crossing is a reviewable piece of source rather than a
; generated one, which is the argument `flight/` already makes for being a hand-written
; transcription held to a reference (`docs/MODELS.md` 47.6).
(library
 (name retrainer)
 (modes native)
 (foreign_stubs
  (language c)
  (names retrainer_stubs)))
